  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.619 acc, a large jump over single-profile multimodal (config_016, 0.527) and RNA-only single-profile (config_001, 0.485). This confirms multi-profile aggregation is the dominant performance driver. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether avgpool is the optimal aggregation strategy or whether a transformer-based aggregation (which can model inter-profile relationships) would further improve performance. config_020 is a clean single-variable change from config_018 (avgpool → transformer, all else identical), directly testing whether more expressive profile aggregation yields gains. This is the best next experiment because it exploits our strongest finding (multi-profile is critical) while resolving a key design-axis uncertainty with minimal confounding, and the result will inform whether to invest further in aggregation complexity or pivot to other dimensions (fusion strategy, encoder quality)."
}

